---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How often should I export DNS records?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Before any planned change, after any provider switch, and quarterly as a routine backup for business-critical domains."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Can I import an exported zone file?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Yes: BIND-format zone files import into most providers (Cloudflare, Route 53). Format-specific exports may need conversion."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What if I lose my DKIM keys?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Regenerate them from your email provider (they create new key pairs), then update the DNS record. Old mail signed with the old key will fail until the new one propagates."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Is there a tool to capture all records at once?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Yes: our all-in-one record lookup queries every type in one pass. Screenshot or copy the output as your backup."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Should I back up nameservers too?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Yes: note which nameservers your registrar points at. This delegation is separate from the zone records."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How do I restore records after a mistake?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Use your export as a reference and re-create the records in your DNS panel. Verification with the record lookup confirms restoration."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout
  title="How to Export and Back Up DNS Records"
  description="export dns records backup"
  schema={[faqSchema]}
 breadcrumb={[["Home", "/"], ["DNS Guide", "/dns/"], ["How to Export and Back Up DNS Records"]]}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/dns/" class="hover:text-accent">DNS Guide</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">How to Export and Back Up DNS Records</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">How to Export and Back Up DNS Records</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Export your DNS records before any migration or provider switch: methods for every major provider and a manual fallback.</p>
    </div>
<nav class="pd-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent">On this page</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#why-export-before-changes">Why export before changes</a></li>
        <li><a href="#export-methods-by-provider">Export methods by provider</a></li>
        <li><a href="#what-to-include-in-your-backup">What to include in your backup</a></li>
        <li><a href="#frequently-asked-questions">Frequently asked questions</a></li>
        <li><a href="#related">Related</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="why-export-before-changes">Why export before changes</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li class="leading-relaxed">A backup lets you restore records instantly if a migration goes wrong.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">It captures verification tokens and DKIM keys you might otherwise lose.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">It’s the reference document for rebuilding the zone at a new provider.</li></ul>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="export-methods-by-provider">Export methods by provider</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60"><table class="pdns-table"><tbody><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Cloudflare</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Export button in DNS, Records (downloads a BIND zone file)</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Route 53</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Console: hosted zone, Export (or AWS CLI list-resource-record-sets)</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">GoDaddy</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">No native export: screenshot the records table or use DNS lookup to capture values</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Namecheap</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">No native export: use Advanced DNS page or our record lookup per type</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Manual fallback</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Run a record lookup for each type (A, MX, TXT, CNAME...) and save the output</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="what-to-include-in-your-backup">What to include in your backup</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li class="leading-relaxed">All record types: A, AAAA, CNAME, MX, TXT (SPF, DKIM, DMARC), NS, CAA.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">TTL values: they matter for the migration window.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Priority values for MX and SRV records.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">The nameserver set at the registrar (delegation, not just the zone).</li></ul>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="frequently-asked-questions">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How often should I export DNS records?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Before any planned change, after any provider switch, and quarterly as a routine backup for business-critical domains.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I import an exported zone file?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes: BIND-format zone files import into most providers (Cloudflare, Route 53). Format-specific exports may need conversion.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What if I lose my DKIM keys?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Regenerate them from your email provider (they create new key pairs), then update the DNS record. Old mail signed with the old key will fail until the new one propagates.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Is there a tool to capture all records at once?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes: our all-in-one record lookup queries every type in one pass. Screenshot or copy the output as your backup.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Should I back up nameservers too?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes: note which nameservers your registrar points at. This delegation is separate from the zone records.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I restore records after a mistake?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Use your export as a reference and re-create the records in your DNS panel. Verification with the record lookup confirms restoration.</p></details></div>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="related">Related</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2"><li><a href="/dns-migration-checklist/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DNS migration checklist →</a></li><li><a href="/dns-record-lookup/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">Record lookup →</a></li><li><a href="/what-is-ttl-in-dns/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">TTL explained →</a></li></ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
